DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The  nneexxttaafftteerr(),  nneexxttaafftteerrff(),  and nneexxttaafftteerrll() functions return the
       next representable floating‐point value following _x in the direction of
       _y.  If _y is less than _x, these functions will return the largest repre‐
       sentable number less than _x.

       If _x equals _y, the functions return _y.

       The nneexxttttoowwaarrdd(), nneexxttttoowwaarrddff(), and  nneexxttttoowwaarrddll()  functions  do  the
       same  as the corresponding nneexxttaafftteerr() functions, except that they have
       a _l_o_n_g _d_o_u_b_l_e second argument.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       On success, these functions return  the  next  representable  floating‐
       point value after _x in the direction of _y.

       If _x equals _y, then _y (cast to the same type as _x) is returned.

       If _x or _y is a NaN, a NaN is returned.

       If  _x  is  finite, and the result would overflow, a range error occurs,
       and the functions return HHUUGGEE__VVAALL,  HHUUGGEE__VVAALLFF,  or  HHUUGGEE__VVAALLLL,  respec‐
       tively, with the correct mathematical sign.

       If  _x  is not equal to _y, and the correct function result would be sub‐
       normal, zero, or underflow, a range error occurs, and either  the  cor‐
       rect value (if it can be represented), or 0.0, is returned.

